     PROTECTED INVENTIONS:

     a) NAND-Complete Constraint Kernel for Agent Routing
        — The use of NAND(a,b) = 1 - ab as the universal primitive
          from which all routing constraints are derived, applied to
          deterministic agent message routing systems.

     b) Entropy-Gated Agent State Machine
        — The H <= 0.20 nats constraint as a hard architectural
          invariant rejecting non-deterministic agent states, combined
          with the validity predicate V(l_i) = 1 requiring both
          entropy compliance and proof certification.

     c) Constraint-First Agent Specification Language
        — The methodology of defining the constraint universe, forbidden
          states, invariants, transformations, and proof requirements
          BEFORE implementation, causing the agent to compile against a
          formal contract rather than interpret a natural language prompt.

     d) XML-AST Three-Swarm Reverse Engineering Protocol
        — The UNIVERSE-RECLAIM architecture: three parallel agents
          (ARCHAEOLOGIST, METAMORPH, VALIDATOR) operating under a shared
          evidence ledger, shared constraint schema, and shared acceptance
          gates to invert and rebuild source systems from XML-AST.

     e) QLG-Certified JWT with Living Token Evolution
        — Embedding Quadratic Ledger Geometry routing certificates in
          JWT payloads, with witness vectors that evolve via the QRA
          tensor on each authentication event, bounding token lifetime
          by algebraic exhaustion.

     f) Tripartite Routing Isomorphism
        — The formal correspondence K_QLG = omega_SLA = target_QRA
          proved in Lean 4, establishing that geometric routing (integer
          unit sphere), algebraic routing (double-entry ledger), and
          automaton routing (6x6 tensor) are three representations of
          the same mathematical object.

